NAME: Vendor review
OWNER: Vendor Scout
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Thursdays at 9:13 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Vendor review" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Vendor review · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Vendor review · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Vendor review · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Vendor review · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Vendor review · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/vendor-scout/ that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-vendor-scout.md yet, record it with the vendor-review skill (recompute the sha256 of the pending item's payload and match it to the decision's HASH; yes: note "approved, Tommy sends it" and tell TMEC Command, and log it as sent only when Tommy says he sent it; no: mark it declined; change: redraft once as a new item), and add the id and the outcome to the sent keys so a no or a change is never read again. TMEC Command may already have nudged you in your own chat; this is the fallback. You send nothing yourself, so there is nothing outward to gate. In test mode (this routine is listed test, or config.json run is test), write what you would have drafted to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/ and start item ids with test-.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-vendor-scout/ and do it first.
Then, if `vendor_scout` in /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is "on", use the vendor-review skill for the weekly review. If nothing changed since last week (no new term on a public page, no new candidate, no figure that moved past a vendor's or Tommy's line, no reply recorded), write NO_CHANGE and stop; message no one.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/vendor-scout.md: what changed, drafts waiting on Tommy, anything blocked and why. Send nothing to anyone but Tommy.
